--- a/docs/BACKUP_RECOVERY.md
+++ b/docs/BACKUP_RECOVERY.md
@@ -45,6 +45,13 @@ AES-256-GCM, key derived from `NEXUS_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE` with scrypt; chunk order
 Mandatory for remote destinations; optional for local ones (`"encrypt": true`). The snapshot manifest (file names) is
 encrypted too. **There is no passphrase recovery.**
 
+## Off-machine copy without a new account
+The `git-private-branch` destination pushes the encrypted `state` + `metadata` tiers to a branch of a private Git
+repository (see `docs/STORAGE.md`). After a machine loss: clone the code, put the same destination entry in
+`.nexus/storage.json`, set the passphrase, `python -m nexus restore .nexus-restored --from offsite`. You get back every
+project, timeline, script and QA report; media comes from a media-capable destination (external drive / B2 / Drive) and
+anything it cannot find is listed under `references.missing` — never silently skipped.
+
 ## Known limits
 - A backup is queued automatically every 24 h while the app runs (`"backup_every_hours"` in `settings.json`, 0 = off). Old snapshots are not pruned automatically yet (`nexus` has `backup.prune`; task STO-4).
 - Content hashes are visible to the storage provider as object names (they reveal nothing but equality of files).
