 Without this file there is one destination: `NEXUS_HOME/backups` — same disk, so it protects against mistakes, **not**
 against losing the disk. `nexus status` and the UI say so.
 
+### Recommended external backup strategy (zero accounts to create)
+| Copy | Destination | Holds | Why |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `local` (same disk) | everything | instant undo of mistakes |
+| 2 | **`offsite` Git branch `nexus-backup`** of this private repo, encrypted | database, timelines, reports, settings | survives loss of the machine; uses credentials you already have |
+| 3 | external drive / NAS (`local` provider, another path) **or** Backblaze B2 / Google Drive via rclone | originals, narration, licensed assets | media is too large for Git |
+
+Enable copy 2 by adding this to `.nexus/storage.json` and setting `NEXUS_BACKUP_PASSPHRASE`:
+```json
+{"name": "offsite", "provider": "git-private-branch", "url": "https://github.com/<you>/<private-repo>.git",
+ "branch": "nexus-backup", "authorized": true, "enabled": true}
+```
+`"authorized": true` is your consent to push encrypted project data to that branch. Then `NEXUS_BACKUP.bat` — it pushes,
+re-reads the remote branch, compares checksums and runs a restore drill. Restoring on a new machine needs only the repo
+URL and the passphrase. **Status:** proven end to end against a separate Git remote in
+`tests/fast/test_storage_backup.py::test_offsite_git_backup_restores_on_a_fresh_machine`; **not yet run against
+github.com**, because pushing a new branch with your data needs your go-ahead (task `STO-3`).
+
+Limits: Git keeps every old database snapshot in history, so NEXUS caps this destination at 0.45 GB and reports when it
+is full (then: start a fresh branch name). It never stores media there.
+
 ### Add a remote destination (user action — an agent must never create accounts)
 1. Create the free account **without adding a payment method**. For B2: create a private bucket and an application key limited to it.
 2. `rclone config` → new remote (e.g. `nexusb2`). Credentials are stored by rclone, outside the repository.
