index 0000000..baddc99
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/GENERATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,83 @@
+# Image & Video Generation — research, benchmarks, selection (2026-11-12)
+
+**Bottom line.** On the build machine (4 CPU threads, 15.6 GB RAM, **no GPU**) NEXUS now generates real images, real
+camera movement and short real text-to-video clips, all with commercially usable open weights. That lifts
+"create from zero" from a slideshow to directed, generated shots. It is **not cinematic video generation**: the strong
+video models (Wan, LTX, HunyuanVideo, CogVideoX) need a GPU that this machine does not have, and none of them was run
+here. They are registered, licence-checked and ranked so that the moment a free GPU is authorised the selector routes to
+them — but their adapter is not written yet (task `GEN-2`).
+
+Reproduce every number: `python scripts/bench_generation.py image|video` → `docs/results/gen_bench_*.json`.
+What this machine will use: `python -m nexus genmodels`.
+
+## 1. Measured on this machine
+### Images
+| Candidate | Licence (model card) | Size | Steps | s / image | Peak RAM | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `sd15-dreamshaper-lcm` (Lykon/dreamshaper-8 + LCM-LoRA) | CreativeML OpenRAIL-M + OpenRAIL++ | 512×288 | 5 | **13.8** | 5.5 GB | fast preview |
+| same | | 768×432 | 5 | **32.7** | 6.3 GB | **default** — clean compositions, convincing portraits and scenes |
+| `tiny-sd-lcm` (segmind/tiny-sd) | CreativeML OpenRAIL-M | — | — | failed | — | **rejected**: pruned UNet cannot load the LCM-LoRA (shape mismatch) |
+| `ssd1b-lcm` (segmind/SSD-1B, 1024 px) | Apache-2.0 + OpenRAIL++ | — | — | not run | — | registered; not a default until measured |
+
+Inspected by eye (harbour scene, sea-captain portrait, virus illustration): coherent, well lit, usable as shots. Weaknesses:
+soft when upscaled to 720p (measured sharpness about half of a 1920 px stock photo), garbled text, occasional anatomy errors.
+
+### Video
+| Technique | Licence | Output | Time | Peak RAM | What it really is |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `animatediff-lightning-4step` text-to-video | CreativeML OpenRAIL-M | 16 frames 384×216 (2 s @ 8 fps) | **71.5 s** | 12.9 GB | real generated motion |
+| same, 512×288, no memory slicing | | — | — | **out of memory** (process killed) | |
+| same, 512×288, VAE + attention slicing | | 16 frames (2 s) | **115 s** | 11.0 GB | **default** for the opening "motion shot" |
+| `depth-parallax` camera move (Depth Anything V2 Small) | Apache-2.0 | 120 frames 1280×720 (4 s @ 30 fps) | **1.5 s** (+4 s first load) | < 2 GB | real camera movement with depth parallax over a still; subjects do not move |
+
+Inspected by eye: the AnimateDiff clip is coherent motion (a boat drifting, mist moving) but short, soft and loop-like —
+a stop-gap. The parallax shots show true foreground/background separation and are cheap enough for every scene.
+
+## 2. Candidates that need a GPU (NOT run here — licences read from the model cards, hardware figures as reported upstream)
+| Model | Kind | Licence | Commercial | Reported VRAM | Native output | Selector status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **Wan 2.2 TI2V-5B** | text + image → video | Apache-2.0 | yes | ~8 GB quantised/offloaded; upstream README says 24 GB unquantised | 720p, 5 s @ 24 fps | **first choice** for a free 16 GB GPU |
+| **Wan 2.1 T2V-1.3B** | text → video | Apache-2.0 | yes | ~8.2 GB | 480p, 5 s @ 16 fps | fallback on 8 GB |
+| CogVideoX-2b | text → video | Apache-2.0 | yes | ~8 GB | 720×480, 6 s @ 8 fps | older fallback |
+| Mochi 1 | text → video | Apache-2.0 | yes | 20 GB+ | 480p | too large for free GPUs |
+| **LTX-2** (and 2.3/2.5) | text + image → video + audio, multi-shot | LTX-2 Community License | **conditional**: free under USD 10 M annual revenue, use restrictions | 16 GB+ (one source: 32 GB) | up to 4K | strongest per public reports; needs opt-in |
+| LTX-Video 0.9.x | text + image → video | custom ("other") | conditional | ~8 GB | 768×512 | opt-in |
+| CogVideoX-5b | text → video | CogVideoX licence | conditional | ~12 GB | 720×480 | opt-in |
+| HunyuanVideo 1.5 | text + image → video | Tencent Hunyuan Community | **conditional + territory**: licence does not apply in the EU, UK, South Korea | ~14 GB with offloading | 720p | never selected without explicit territory opt-in |
+| Stable Video Diffusion | image → video | Stability community | conditional | ~10 GB | 576×1024, 2–4 s | superseded |
+| Z-Image-Turbo / FLUX.2 klein 4B / Qwen-Image | image | Apache-2.0 | yes | 8 / 12 / 16 GB+ | 1024 px+ | GPU image upgrades |
+| SDXL-Turbo | image | Stability **non-commercial** | **no** | — | — | rejected |
+
+Why not judge by popularity: HunyuanVideo and LTX-2 are among the best-looking open models, yet one is unusable for a
+creator in the EU/UK/Korea and the other is conditionally licensed — so the automatic first choice is Wan 2.2 5B, whose
+licence is unconditional. Why nothing bigger runs locally: Wan's text encoder alone (UMT5-XXL, ~5.7 B parameters) needs
+more memory than this machine can give it at a usable speed.
+
+## 3. Model + compute selection (`nexus/generate/select.py`, registry `nexus/registry/genmodels.yaml`)
+Order: licence eligible → fits a free compute tier → higher quality → measured here. Rules enforced in code and tests:
+- non-commercial licences are never selectable; conditional licences need the model id in `accepted_conditional_licenses`
+  (settings.json); territory-restricted licences need a separate explicit opt-in;
+- a model becomes a default only after it has been **benchmarked on real hardware**;
+- a model is "runnable" only where NEXUS has a working adapter — GPU models are listed under *better with* together
+  with what they need and where they could run, never claimed to work;
+- remote free compute (Kaggle: ~30 GPU-hours/week, 16 GB T4) is considered only after `"compute": {"kaggle": true}`.
+
+On this machine today: image → `sd15-dreamshaper-lcm` (CPU); text-to-video → `animatediff-lightning-4step` (CPU);
+camera move → `depth-parallax`; image-to-video → **not available** (no eligible model fits a CPU).
+
+## 4. How generation is used in productions (`nexus/generate/shots.py`)
+- Each scene gets a **shot list**, not one still: scenes longer than 9 s get a wide and a closer shot; the first scene
+  opens with a generated moving clip when the machine has ≥ 14 GB RAM.
+- Every shot gets a camera move with depth parallax (push-in, pull-out, pan, rise, orbit), chosen by the style preset.
+- Factual content prefers a licensed photo **only if its title is really about the scene** (relevance ≥ 0.5); otherwise
+  the picture is generated from the script's `visual_prompt` (a full-sentence description written with the narration).
+- Nine style presets (cinematic, documentary, educational, scientific, commercial, storytelling, social, explainer, film)
+  set prompt language, camera moves, grade and music mood.
+- Every generated shot records model, licence, prompt and seed; results are cached, so re-rendering or regenerating
+  one scene costs nothing for the others.
+
+## 5. What is still missing for "cinematic"
+1. A GPU adapter + a real free GPU (Kaggle) run of Wan 2.2 TI2V-5B: text-to-video and image-to-video at 720p (`GEN-2`, blocked on the user's account).
+2. Identity-preserving character generation (IP-Adapter or reference-image editing models); today consistency comes from fixed descriptions + seeds and is only approximate.
+3. Sharper stills: SSD-1B/SDXL at 1024 px on CPU is unmeasured; a GPU image model (Z-Image-Turbo, FLUX.2 klein) is the real fix.
+4. VFX/compositing, upscaling and frame interpolation models (`GEN-3`).
diff --git a/nexus/bench.py b/nexus/bench.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9256127
--- /dev/null
+++ b/nexus/bench.py
@@ -0,0 +1,260 @@
+"""Quality benchmark + regression: fixed production examples, measured the same way every time, compared with a
+saved baseline. `python -m nexus regress run` fails (exit 1) when a meaningful metric gets worse.
+
+What is measured (all from the rendered file, the timeline and the script - nothing is self-reported by a model):
+  visual      sharpness, colourfulness, share of scenes with a real picture (not a title card)
+  motion      mean frame-to-frame change, share of the programme that is a frozen picture, generated-motion shots, shots per scene
+  story       words per scene, sentence count, hook present, source grounding / QA gates passed
+  continuity  cuts per minute, repeated visuals
+  voice       Whisper hears the narration back (share of script words recovered)
+  translation back-translation similarity + language QA checks (localised case)
+  audio       integrated loudness, true peak, dead air
+  subtitles   cues, longest cue, reading speed, cues that straddle a sentence boundary
+  technical   codec/resolution/fps, decode errors, black/frozen sections, duration vs timeline
+
+These are proxies. They catch regressions and prove direction (e.g. "no longer a slideshow"); they do not replace
+a person watching the result."""
+from __future__ import annotations
+
+import json
+import re
+import subprocess
+import time
+from pathlib import Path
+
+from . import config
+
+RESULTS = config.ROOT / "docs" / "results" / "bench"
+BASELINE = RESULTS / "baseline.json"
+
+# metric -> (direction, tolerance). "up": must not fall by more than tol (relative); "down": must not rise by more than
+# tol (relative, with a small absolute floor); "eq": must match exactly; "near": absolute distance to baseline <= tol.
+RULES: dict[str, tuple[str, float]] = {
+    "visual.sharpness": ("up", 0.35), "visual.colorfulness": ("up", 0.40), "visual.real_picture_ratio": ("up", 0.15),
+    "motion.mean_change": ("up", 0.35), "motion.frozen_ratio": ("down", 0.25), "motion.generated_motion_shots": ("up", 0.0),
+    "motion.shots_per_scene": ("up", 0.25),
+    "story.min_words_per_scene": ("up", 0.35), "story.gates_passed_ratio": ("up", 0.10), "story.hook": ("up", 0.0),
+    "continuity.repeated_visuals": ("down", 0.0),
+    "voice.heard_back": ("up", 0.12), "translation.back_similarity": ("up", 0.15), "translation.checks_passed_ratio": ("up", 0.15),
+    "audio.lufs": ("near", 1.5), "audio.true_peak": ("down", 0.0), "audio.dead_air_s": ("down", 0.5),
+    "subtitles.straddling_cues": ("down", 0.0), "subtitles.max_chars": ("down", 0.10), "subtitles.max_cps": ("down", 0.25),
+    "technical.decode_errors": ("eq", 0), "technical.black_s": ("down", 0.5), "technical.width": ("eq", 0), "technical.height": ("eq", 0),
+    "technical.fps": ("eq", 0), "technical.qa_passed": ("up", 0.0),
+}
+
+
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------- measuring one programme
+def _frames(path: str | Path, fps: float = 2.0, w: int = 320, h: int = 180):
+    import numpy as np
+    r = subprocess.run(["ffmpeg", "-loglevel", "error", "-i", str(path), "-vf", f"fps={fps},scale={w}:{h}", "-pix_fmt", "rgb24", "-f", "rawvideo", "-"],
+                       capture_output=True)
+    a = np.frombuffer(r.stdout, dtype=np.uint8)
+    n = len(a) // (w * h * 3)
+    return a[: n * w * h * 3].reshape(n, h, w, 3).astype("float32") if n else np.zeros((0, h, w, 3), dtype="float32")
+
+
+def picture_metrics(path: str | Path) -> dict:
+    import numpy as np
+    f = _frames(path)
+    if len(f) < 2:
+        return {"sharpness": 0.0, "colorfulness": 0.0, "mean_change": 0.0, "frozen_ratio": 1.0}
+    g = f.mean(axis=3)
+    lap = g[:, 1:-1, 1:-1] * 4 - g[:, :-2, 1:-1] - g[:, 2:, 1:-1] - g[:, 1:-1, :-2] - g[:, 1:-1, 2:]
+    rg, yb = f[..., 0] - f[..., 1], 0.5 * (f[..., 0] + f[..., 1]) - f[..., 2]
+    color = np.sqrt(rg.std(axis=(1, 2)) ** 2 + yb.std(axis=(1, 2)) ** 2) + 0.3 * np.sqrt(rg.mean(axis=(1, 2)) ** 2 + yb.mean(axis=(1, 2)) ** 2)
+    diff = np.abs(g[1:] - g[:-1]).mean(axis=(1, 2))
+    return {"sharpness": round(float(np.median(lap.var(axis=(1, 2)))), 1), "colorfulness": round(float(np.median(color)), 1),
+            # half-second steps whose picture barely changes = a still on screen (subtitle changes alone stay under 0.25)
+            "mean_change": round(float(diff.mean()), 3), "frozen_ratio": round(float((diff < 0.25).mean()), 3)}
+
+
+def timeline_metrics(tl: dict) -> dict:
+    scenes = [c for c in tl["clips"] if c.get("narration")]
+    real = [c for c in scenes if c.get("shots") or (c["type"] in ("image", "video") and "title-card" not in str((c.get("provenance") or {}).get("source", "")))]
+    shots = sum(len(c.get("shots") or [1]) for c in scenes)
+    gen_motion = sum(1 for c in scenes for s in c.get("shots") or [] if s.get("kind") == "generated-video")
+    imgs = [s.get("image") for c in scenes for s in (c.get("shots") or []) if s.get("image")] + [c["src"] for c in scenes if c["type"] == "image"]
+    return {"scenes": len(scenes), "real_picture_ratio": round(len(real) / max(1, len(scenes)), 3), "shots_per_scene": round(shots / max(1, len(scenes)), 2),
+            "generated_motion_shots": gen_motion, "repeated_visuals": len(imgs) - len(set(imgs)),
+            "cuts_per_minute": round(60 * max(0, shots + 1) / max(1.0, sum(float(c.get("duration") or (c.get("out", 0) - c.get("in", 0))) for c in tl["clips"])), 1)}
+
+
+def subtitle_metrics(tl: dict) -> dict:
+    cues = tl.get("subtitles") or []
+    if not cues:
+        return {"cues": 0, "max_chars": 0, "max_cps": 0.0, "straddling_cues": 0}
+    return {"cues": len(cues), "max_chars": max(len(c["text"]) for c in cues),
+            "max_cps": round(max(len(c["text"]) / max(0.3, c["end"] - c["start"]) for c in cues), 1),
+            "straddling_cues": sum(1 for c in cues if re.search(r"[.!?]\s+\S", c["text"]))}
+
+
+def story_metrics(script: dict, report: dict | None) -> dict:
+    sc = script.get("scenes", [])
+    words = [len(s["narration"].split()) for s in sc] or [0]
+    hook = sc[0]["narration"] if sc else ""
+    pre = next((s for s in (report or {}).get("stages", []) if s["stage"] == "1-pre-production"), None)
+    checks = pre["checks"] if pre else []
+    return {"scenes": len(sc), "words": sum(words), "min_words_per_scene": min(words),
+            "sentences_per_scene": round(sum(len(re.findall(r"[.!?](?:\s|$)", s["narration"])) for s in sc) / max(1, len(sc)), 2),
+            "hook": int("?" in hook or bool(re.search(r"\d|never|every|most|only|imagine|did you", hook, re.I))),
+            "gates_passed_ratio": round(sum(c["ok"] for c in checks) / len(checks), 3) if checks else 0.0}
+
+
+def voice_metric(video: str | Path, script: dict, lang: str = "en") -> dict:
+    """Transcribe the finished programme's audio and compare with the script: is the narration intelligible in the mix?"""
+    from . import qa
+    from .media import ff
+    from .speech import asr
+    wav = Path(video).with_suffix(".bench.wav")
+    ff.extract_audio(video, wav)
+    heard = asr.transcribe(wav, language=lang.split("-")[0], words=False)["text"]
+    wav.unlink(missing_ok=True)
+    return {"heard_back": round(qa.text_similarity(" ".join(s["narration"] for s in script["scenes"]), heard), 3)}
+
+
+def measure(video: str | Path, tl: dict | None = None, script: dict | None = None, report: dict | None = None, voice: bool = True, lang: str = "en") -> dict:
+    from .media import ff
+    info = ff.probe(video)
+    loud = ff.loudness(video)
+    silences = ff.detect_silence(video, min_dur=2.5)
+    tech = next((s for s in (report or {}).get("stages", []) if s["stage"] == "5-technical"), None)
+    pm = picture_metrics(video)
+    m: dict = {
+        "visual": {"sharpness": pm["sharpness"], "colorfulness": pm["colorfulness"]},
+        "motion": {"mean_change": pm["mean_change"], "frozen_ratio": pm["frozen_ratio"]},
+        "audio": {"lufs": round(float(loud.get("input_i", loud.get("lufs", 0))), 2), "true_peak": round(float(loud.get("input_tp", loud.get("true_peak", 0))), 2),
+                  "dead_air_s": round(sum(b - a for a, b in silences), 2)},
+        "technical": {"duration": round(info["duration"], 2), "width": info["video"]["width"], "height": info["video"]["height"], "fps": info["video"]["fps"],
+                      "decode_errors": len(ff.decode_check(video)), "black_s": round(sum(b - a for a, b in ff.detect_black(video)), 2),
+                      "qa_passed": int(bool(tech and tech["passed"])) if report else 0},
+    }
+    if tl:
+        t = timeline_metrics(tl)
+        m["visual"]["real_picture_ratio"] = t["real_picture_ratio"]
+        m["motion"].update(generated_motion_shots=t["generated_motion_shots"], shots_per_scene=t["shots_per_scene"])
+        m["continuity"] = {"repeated_visuals": t["repeated_visuals"], "cuts_per_minute": t["cuts_per_minute"], "scenes": t["scenes"]}
+        m["subtitles"] = subtitle_metrics(tl)
+    if script:
+        m["story"] = story_metrics(script, report)
+        if voice:
+            m["voice"] = voice_metric(video, script, lang)
+    return m
+
+
+def measure_project(pid: str, render: str = "master", branch: str = "main", voice: bool = True) -> dict:
+    from . import project as prj
+    p = prj.Project(pid)
+    rep = p.dir / "reports" / f"{render}.qa.json"
+    return measure(p.dir / "renders" / f"{render}.mp4", p.timeline(branch), p.data.get("script"), json.loads(rep.read_text()) if rep.exists() else None, voice,
+                   p.timeline(branch).get("lang", "en"))
+
+
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------- fixed cases
+NOTES_SOLAR = ("Solar panels convert sunlight directly into electricity using photovoltaic cells made of silicon. When light hits a cell it knocks electrons loose, "
+               "and the cell's electric field pushes them into a current. In the last decade the price of solar electricity fell by almost 90 percent, which made "
+               "it the cheapest source of new electricity in most countries. The main challenge is storage, because the sun does not shine at night. Batteries "
+               "store surplus daytime power and release it in the evening, and their cost is falling quickly as well.")
+
+
+def case_explainer(stage=None) -> dict:
+    """Fixed create-from-idea production: same topic, same notes, same scene count, same preset."""
+    from . import create
+    t0 = time.time()
+    r = create.create_video("How solar panels make electricity", scenes=3, notes=NOTES_SOLAR, name="BENCH explainer-solar", preset="documentary",
+                            visuals="auto", motion_shots=1, stage=stage)
+    m = measure_project(r["project"])
+    m["performance"] = {"total_s": round(time.time() - t0, 1), "render_s": r["render"]["elapsed"]}
+    return {"case": "explainer-solar", "project": r["project"], "output": r["output"], "metrics": m}
+
+
+def case_localized(source_project: str, lang: str = "de") -> dict:
+    """Fixed localisation of the explainer: translation fidelity, dubbed voice intelligibility, translated subtitles."""
+    from . import localize, project as prj, qa
+    t0 = time.time()
+    p = prj.Project(source_project)
+    ltl, review = localize.localize(p, p.timeline("main"), lang, None, context=p.name, dub=True)
+    p.save_timeline(ltl, f"{lang} version", branch=lang)
+    stats, report = qa.render_with_qa(p, ltl, f"bench_{lang}", extra_stages=[review], extra={"language": lang})
+    script = {"scenes": [{"narration": c["narration"]} for c in ltl["clips"] if c.get("narration")]}
+    m = measure(stats["output"], ltl, script, report, voice=True, lang=lang)
+    m.pop("story", None)
+    back = next((c for c in review["checks"] if c["check"].startswith("back-translation")), None)
+    sims = re.findall(r"(\d+)%", back["detail"]) if back else []
+    automatic = [c for c in review["checks"] if not c["check"].startswith("native-speaker")]
+    m["translation"] = {"checks_passed_ratio": round(sum(c["ok"] for c in automatic) / max(1, len(automatic)), 3),
+                        "back_similarity": round(int(sims[0]) / 100, 2) if sims else (1.0 if back and back["ok"] else 0.0),  # mean overlap
+                        "lines": len(review.get("lines", [])), "native_review": "required - not automated"}
+    m["performance"] = {"total_s": round(time.time() - t0, 1)}
+    return {"case": f"localized-{lang}", "project": source_project, "output": stats["output"], "metrics": m}
+
+
+CASES = ("explainer-solar", "localized-de")
+
+
+def run(cases: list[str] | None = None) -> dict:
+    out, src = {}, None
+    for name in cases or CASES:
+        if name == "explainer-solar":
+            r = case_explainer()
+            src = r["project"]
+        elif name.startswith("localized-"):
+            if src is None:
+                src = case_explainer()["project"] if "explainer-solar" not in out else out["explainer-solar"]["project"]
+            r = case_localized(src, name.split("-", 1)[1])
+        else:
+            raise KeyError(f"unknown benchmark case {name}")
+        out[r["case"]] = r
+    RESULTS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
+    cur = {"date": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%d"), "nexus_version": config.VERSION, "cases": {k: v["metrics"] for k, v in out.items()}}
+    (RESULTS / "current.json").write_text(json.dumps(cur, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
+    return {"current": cur, "outputs": {k: v["output"] for k, v in out.items()}}
+
+
+# ----------------------------------------------------------------- comparing with the baseline
+def flatten(m: dict) -> dict[str, float]:
+    return {f"{g}.{k}": v for g, d in m.items() if isinstance(d, dict) for k, v in d.items() if isinstance(v, (int, float))}
+
+
+def compare(current: dict, baseline: dict) -> dict:
+    """Per case: regressions (rule violated), improvements, unchanged. Only metrics with a rule can fail the run."""
+    res = {"ok": True, "cases": {}}
+    for case, cm in current["cases"].items():
+        bm = baseline.get("cases", {}).get(case)
+        if bm is None:
+            res["cases"][case] = {"status": "new (no baseline)", "regressions": [], "improvements": []}
+            continue
+        c, b = flatten(cm), flatten(bm)
+        reg, imp = [], []
+        for key, (direction, tol) in RULES.items():
+            if key not in c or key not in b:
+                continue
+            cv, bv = c[key], b[key]
+            if direction == "eq":
+                bad, good = cv != bv, False
+            elif direction == "near":
+                bad, good = abs(cv - bv) > tol, False
+            elif direction == "up":
+                bad, good = cv < bv - abs(bv) * tol - 1e-9, cv > bv + abs(bv) * max(tol, 0.1) + 1e-9
+            else:  # down
+                floor = max(abs(bv) * tol, tol if abs(bv) < 1 else 0.0)
+                bad, good = cv > bv + floor + 1e-9, cv < bv - max(abs(bv) * max(tol, 0.1), 1e-9)
+            if bad:
+                reg.append({"metric": key, "baseline": bv, "current": cv, "rule": f"{direction} (tolerance {tol})"})
+            elif good:
+                imp.append({"metric": key, "baseline": bv, "current": cv})
+        res["cases"][case] = {"status": "REGRESSED" if reg else "ok", "regressions": reg, "improvements": imp}
+        res["ok"] &= not reg
+    return res
+
+
+def accept(note: str = "") -> dict:
+    """Promote the current results to be the baseline (the previous baseline is kept in history)."""
+    cur = json.loads((RESULTS / "current.json").read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
+    hist = RESULTS / "history.json"
+    h = json.loads(hist.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) if hist.exists() else []
+    if BASELINE.exists():
+        h.append(json.loads(BASELINE.read_text(encoding="utf-8")))
+    hist.write_text(json.dumps(h[-20:], indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
+    cur["note"] = note
+    BASELINE.write_text(json.dumps(cur, indent=1) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
+    return cur
